    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">absŏlūtōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to acquittal</i>, <i>release.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabellae, damnatoria et absolutoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicia, Gai,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					4, 114</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">absŏlūtōrĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n. (sc. remedium), <i>a means of deliverance from</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ejus mali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 6, 17, § 63</span></i>
			.</div>
